{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/audio/ovi-english-beginner-2026-07-01-horse-riding-basics-a1.mp3","durationSec":283.872,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.4,"text":"Horse riding means sitting on a horse and moving with the horse."},{"start":4.3,"end":5.62,"text":"Some people ride for fun."},{"start":6.36,"end":7.52,"text":"Some people ride in lessons."},{"start":8.36,"end":9.64,"text":"Some people ride as a sport."},{"start":10.44,"end":13.5,"text":"Riding can feel exciting, but it can also feel calm."},{"start":14.58,"end":15.6,"text":"Have you ever seen a horse?"},{"start":16.5,"end":18.62,"text":"Do you think horse riding looks fun or scary?"},{"start":19.72,"end":21.52,"text":"What safety rule do you know for a sport?"},{"start":22.56,"end":24.78,"text":"Horse riding is not only sitting on a horse."},{"start":25.56,"end":31.04,"text":"A rider learns how to meet the horse, sit well, hold the reins, and listen to the teacher."},{"start":32,"end":33.4,"text":"The horse and rider work together."},{"start":34.24,"end":36.78,"text":"At first, many riders only walk with the horse."},{"start":37.38,"end":39,"text":"Walking is slow and useful."},{"start":39.76,"end":40.86,"text":"The rider learns balance."},{"start":41.7,"end":43.54,"text":"The horse learns that the rider is calm."},{"start":44.54,"end":47.56,"text":"Horses are big and strong, but many horses are gentle."},{"start":48.48,"end":49.82,"text":"A horse can still feel scared."},{"start":50.72,"end":54.88,"text":"A fast hand, a loud voice, or running feet can surprise a horse."},{"start":55.58,"end":58.4,"text":"Before riding, people should move slowly."},{"start":59.1,"end":61,"text":"They can say hello in a quiet voice."},{"start":61.62,"end":63.54,"text":"They can stand where the teacher says."},{"start":64.2,"end":65.7,"text":"They should not run behind the horse."},{"start":66.42,"end":68.36,"text":"This is the first safety lesson."},{"start":69.5,"end":72.2,"text":"A calm rider helps the horse feel calm too."},{"start":73.32,"end":74.82,"text":"A rider sits on a saddle."},{"start":75.68,"end":78.48,"text":"The saddle helps the rider sit in the right place."},{"start":79.5,"end":81.9,"text":"The rider holds the reins with both hands."},{"start":82.78,"end":88.1,"text":"The reins help the rider ask the horse to stop, turn left, or turn right."},{"start":89.2,"end":91.26,"text":"Good riders do not pull hard."},{"start":92.1,"end":93.28,"text":"They use small signals."},{"start":94.16,"end":96.18,"text":"They also use their body and legs."},{"start":97.18,"end":102.82,"text":"In a beginner lesson, the teacher may say, \"Walk,\" \"Stop,\" \"Turn left,\" or \"Turn right."},{"start":103.94,"end":105.06,"text":"Many riders wear a helmet."},{"start":105.76,"end":107.3,"text":"A helmet protects the head."},{"start":108.02,"end":111.54,"text":"Riders also wear shoes or boots that are good for riding."},{"start":112.54,"end":115.16,"text":"They listen to the teacher before they get on the horse."},{"start":115.98,"end":120,"text":"In a lesson, the teacher checks the horse, the saddle, and the rider."},{"start":120.56,"end":122.94,"text":"The teacher can help the rider get on and get off."},{"start":123.38,"end":127.24,"text":"If the rider feels worried, the rider can say, \"Can we go slowly?"},{"start":128.66,"end":130.94,"text":"A jockey is a person who rides a horse in a race."},{"start":131.68,"end":134.04,"text":"Jockeys are light, strong, and skilled."},{"start":134.04,"end":137.42,"text":"They practice balance, timing, and calm thinking."},{"start":138.28,"end":139.94,"text":"A good jockey does not only go fast."},{"start":140.56,"end":144.92,"text":"A horse can feel small signals from the jockey's hands, legs, and body."},{"start":145.88,"end":148.48,"text":"One famous Japanese jockey is Yutaka Take."},{"start":149.2,"end":152.06,"text":"People know him for many big wins and calm riding."},{"start":152.64,"end":156.52,"text":"A famous jockey trains a lot and learns how each horse moves."},{"start":157.22,"end":161.54,"text":"Many people ride horses only for fun, health, or time with animals."},{"start":162.66,"end":166.1,"text":"Practice after you understand the horse and the safety rules."},{"start":166.84,"end":167.82,"text":"Use the patterns above."},{"start":168.1,"end":170.74,"text":"Explain a first riding lesson in five small steps."},{"start":171.58,"end":173.78,"text":"First, meet the horse slowly."},{"start":174.4,"end":176.36,"text":"Next, put on a helmet."},{"start":177.38,"end":178.36,"text":"Then sit on the saddle."},{"start":179.34,"end":181.32,"text":"After that, hold the reins."},{"start":182,"end":184.16,"text":"Finally, walk slowly with the teacher."},{"start":185.16,"end":186.82,"text":"What do a horse and rider do together?"},{"start":187.44,"end":188.44,"text":"They work together."},{"start":189.6,"end":192.5,"text":"Would you like to start with a slow walk or a faster ride?"},{"start":193.42,"end":195.62,"text":"Why should people move slowly near a horse?"},{"start":196.4,"end":199.16,"text":"Because a horse can feel scared if people move too fast."},{"start":200.24,"end":202.28,"text":"What can you do to help an animal feel safe?"},{"start":203.3,"end":205.28,"text":"What do the reins help the rider do?"},{"start":206.12,"end":209,"text":"The reins help the rider ask the horse where to go."},{"start":210,"end":214.9,"text":"Which move sounds easiest: walk, stop, turn left, or turn right?"},{"start":214.9,"end":217.16,"text":"Why do many riders wear a helmet?"},{"start":218.1,"end":219.32,"text":"A helmet protects the head."},{"start":220.24,"end":222.82,"text":"What safety rule feels most important to you?"},{"start":223.64,"end":224.86,"text":"What does a jockey do?"},{"start":225.5,"end":227.06,"text":"A jockey rides a horse in a race."},{"start":228.12,"end":229.66,"text":"Why can a sportsperson become famous?"},{"start":231.26,"end":232.74,"text":"What is the first step in this practice?"},{"start":233.86,"end":235.96,"text":"The first step is to meet the horse slowly."},{"start":236.94,"end":239.06,"text":"Explain your first horse-riding lesson."},{"start":239.62,"end":244.28,"text":"Then change one detail: the feeling, the horse's size, or the first move."},{"start":269.6,"end":272.92,"text":"Horse riding is a sport and a relationship with an animal."},{"start":272.92,"end":278.9,"text":"A good rider moves slowly, listens carefully, and uses small signals."},{"start":279.58,"end":283.16,"text":"Riding can be exciting, but safety comes first."}],"words":[{"text":"horse","start":0,"end":0.16},{"text":"riding","start":0.16,"end":0.48},{"text":"means","start":0.48,"end":0.84},{"text":"sitting","start":0.84,"end":1.32},{"text":"on","start":1.32,"end":1.6},{"text":"a","start":1.6,"end":1.68},{"text":"horse","start":1.68,"end":1.96},{"text":"and","start":1.96,"end":2.48},{"text":"moving","start":2.48,"end":2.8},{"text":"with","start":2.8,"end":3.06},{"text":"the","start":3.06,"end":3.2},{"text":"horse","start":3.2,"end":3.4},{"text":"some","start":4.3,"end":4.56},{"text":"people","start":4.56,"end":4.82},{"text":"ride","start":4.82,"end":5.12},{"text":"for","start":5.12,"end":5.32},{"text":"fun","start":5.32,"end":5.62},{"text":"some","start":6.36,"end":6.56},{"text":"people","start":6.56,"end":6.76},{"text":"ride","start":6.76,"end":7.12},{"text":"in","start":7.12,"end":7.3},{"text":"lessons","start":7.3,"end":7.52},{"text":"some","start":8.36,"end":8.52},{"text":"people","start":8.52,"end":8.7},{"text":"ride","start":8.7,"end":9.06},{"text":"as","start":9.06,"end":9.24},{"text":"a","start":9.24,"end":9.34},{"text":"sport","start":9.34,"end":9.64},{"text":"riding","start":10.44,"end":10.74},{"text":"can","start":10.74,"end":10.98},{"text":"feel","start":10.98,"end":11.2},{"text":"exciting","start":11.2,"end":11.5},{"text":"but","start":11.64,"end":12.48},{"text":"it","start":12.48,"end":12.58},{"text":"can","start":12.58,"end":12.7},{"text"